Subject: Cantor Attention Manifest Refresh P6 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] aa3a26a8-0675-4b77-a9ac-282b160c31b7

& [Why]
  + the P5 workspace can persist and resolve identities but its current inference window repeats every complete object record
  + complete full-body projection preserves accounting only until context capacity refuses it
  + existing receipt logic proves that complete explicit disposition is feasible but is not yet inference-host accessible

& [WhyThisShape]
  + a complete compact manifest preserves existence and individuation while exact materialization spends detail budget only where requested
  + a full-coverage receipt makes selection omission and uncertainty attributable without pretending to observe hidden transformer attention
  + read-only P6 establishes the refresh proof before any later mutation gate relies on it

& [Rejected]
  + silent top-k or relevance clipping because omitted identity would become indistinguishable from nonexistence
  + full object injection forever because cost scales with all object detail
  + stateful opaque attention leases because restart and independent replay would lose their proof
  + adding relationship closure now because current accounting objects do not yet carry admitted typed inter-object edges
